+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only OR MIT
+
+//! G15 user render submission (I04 W8): one DRM_ASAHI_CMD_RENDER whose flags
+//! are exactly `DRM_ASAHI_RENDER_G15_USER`.
+//!
+//! Flow, all inside `Queue::submit` before the job is armed:
+//!
+//! 1. Read and validate the user input and its kernel profile (W9,
+//!    `render_input.rs` / `render_profile.rs`).
+//! 2. Take the device-wide G15 job slot, assemble or reuse the queue's TA and
+//!    3D channels (W5), reserve the profile's native VA windows in the VM.
+//! 3. Build or reuse the per-queue resources (W6 PM pool, FW page list, PB
+//!    descriptor); allocate this pass's resources
+//!    (W6) and the GPU timing record; place, copy and relocate every user
+//!    section.
+//! 4. Lease one event-control/SKU/UMA set per pipe (W5), which arms one
+//!    fence reference per command.
+//! 5. Build Barrier, 3D, InitBuffer and TA (W4 `build_g15_render`) and write
+//!    both SKU streams into their leased slots.
+//! 6. Dump the pass to debugfs `asahi/g15_render_last` (G15RDMP1) when
+//!    `g15_render_dump` or `g15_render_dry_run` is set. With
+//!    `g15_render_dry_run` the submit stops here with ECANCELED: nothing was
+//!    written to a firmware-visible ring or table, and the render UMA pool's
+//!    coherency epoch was not advanced (W8f). An evidence-only profile always
+//!    stops here; a TRIAL profile goes on only while `g15_render_trial` is
+//!    set (W8t, `G15KernelProfile::may_publish`). A published pass appends
+//!    `publish.uma_epoch_frag` / `publish.uma_epoch_ta`, the epoch written
+//!    right before each engine's publication, to its dump.
+//! 7. Write the PB descriptor, queue [Barrier, Fragment] on the 3D WorkQueue
+//!    job and [InitBuffer, Vertex] on the TA one. `QueueJob::run` publishes
+//!    both through `GpuManager::run_g15_selected_render_pair` in
+//!    [`G15_RENDER_PUBLISH_ORDER`], under one q4 pending-submission raise.
+//!
+//! Completion: each pipe's command callback records its error and its
+//! command's inline completion stamp; whichever of the two runs last reads
+//! GPU start/end from the pass's timing record, releases the q4
+//! reservation, fills `g15_user_status` (through the job's `G15UserBusy`
+//! guard, which clears `busy` on its own if the pair never completes),
+//! frees the job slot and sets the fence error, and only then drops its
+//! leases (the last fence reference), so the fence signals after the slot is
+//! free. Per-pass resources drop at that point too, after both pipes retired.
+//!
+//! I09 R5 (`DRM_ASAHI_RENDER_G15_USER_RT`, `g15_render_user_rt`): the pass
+//! has no driver-owned render target and no canary fill; the user payload
+//! addresses a user BO. The fence error is then the only result (the I05 K4
+//! analogue: completion is verified on the TA/3D transports only), and
+//! `G15_READBACK` has no output for the job.
+//!
+//! I09 R3 (`DRM_ASAHI_RENDER_G15_USER_REGS`, `g15_render_user_regs`): nine
+//! ISP/PPP/ZLS/merge/bgobj register values come from the render command
+//! (`fw::g15_render::g15_user_reg_overrides`) and replace the profile's N
+//! entries after each list is emitted; a value that differs from the profile
+//! gets a g15_trace line.
+
